{
 "label": "daily-pattern-line-filter-anchoring-loki-defaults",
 "date": "2026-11-04",
 "set": "pattern-line-filter-anchoring",
 "description": "Pattern line filters keep the lines Loki's matcher accepts (semantics/pattern-line-filter-anchoring). The proxy sends an anchored regexp as a prefilter under |> and VictoriaLogs' extract pipe plus a filter on the extracted fields, so every selected row of a !> goes through extract. Log queries (limit 100) and count_over_time over the nginx access log, an include and an exclude of a pattern that matches half the lines, the Drilldown volume under an exclude (a concrete step per range), a pattern that ends on a literal and so matches no line, and two-literal patterns (A8 matches the GET request lines, A9 ends on a literal and matches none). Run with the control set.",
